-- title:
--   Ghost divisibility forces coefficient divisibility for Witt vectors
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a commutative ring, let $p$ be a natural number that is prime (as a typeclass hypothesis), and assume that the image of $p$ in $S$ is a non-zero-divisor. Let $z$ be a Witt vector over $S$ for the prime $p$, and let $s$ and $M$ be natural numbers. Suppose that for every $n < M$ the $n$-th ghost component $\mathrm{ghost}_n(z) = \sum_{i\le n} p^i z_i^{p^{n-i}}$ lies in the ideal of $S$ generated by $p^s$. The conclusion is that for every $j < M$ the $j$-th Witt coefficient $z_j$ lies in the ideal generated by $p^{s-j}$, where $s-j$ is truncated natural subtraction, so that for $j \ge s$ the assertion is vacuous (the ideal generated by $p^0 = 1$ is all of $S$). Thus divisibility of the first $M$ ghost components by $p^s$ yields $z_j \in p^{s-j}S$ for all $j < M$, with no assumption relating $s$ and $M$.
--
--   This is the Dwork-style recursion relating divisibility of ghost components to divisibility of Witt coordinates, valid whenever $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in the base ring. It is used in the analysis of formal group laws, where it converts congruences satisfied by the ghost components of a Witt vector into congruences on its coefficients, via [`MvFormalGroup.coeff_mem_span_sup_pow_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector_of_slope`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.coeff_mem_span_sup_pow_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector_of_slope).
-- source:
